---
import SectionCover from '../SectionCover.astro';
import MetaPanel from '../MetaPanel.astro';
import Panel from '../Panel.astro';
import Shot from '../Shot.astro';
import WorkflowSection from '../WorkflowSection.astro';
import { BASELINE } from '../../data/site';
import { workflows, atlas } from '../../data/workflows';

interface Props { print?: boolean }
const { print = false } = Astro.props;
const P1 = workflows.filter((w) => w.priority === 1);
const P2 = workflows.filter((w) => w.priority === 2);
const P3 = workflows.filter((w) => w.priority === 3);
const brk = print ? 'print-section-break' : '';
const wfLimits: Record<string, string> = {
  'WF-01': 'In-app brand leakage (RV-12)', 'WF-02': 'Setup spread across tabs', 'WF-03': 'AI import blocked',
  'WF-04': 'Project select first; dual paths', 'WF-05': 'Offline not exercised', 'WF-06': 'Redrill path not exercised',
  'WF-07': 'OCR + report PDF AI-blocked', 'WF-08': 'No confirm gate', 'WF-09': 'Test PDF AI-gated; email not sent',
  'WF-10': 'Invoice XLSX not rendered', 'WF-11': 'Drilling not gated on sign-in', 'WF-12': 'Two incident stores; AI blocked',
  'WF-13': 'Extraction blocked', 'WF-14': 'Recording/AI blocked', 'WF-15': 'Unstructured jsonb', 'WF-16': 'No tiles',
  'WF-17': '—', 'WF-18': 'RBAC tab shallow', 'WF-19': 'Un-zodded config', 'WF-20': 'SharePoint absent',
  'WF-23': 'Worker blocked', 'WF-24': 'Outlook blocked',
};
---
<!-- 00 READ FIRST -->
<section class={brk} id="g00">
<SectionCover num="00" title="Read First" kicker="Screenshots & Workflow Guide · runtime companion">
  The visual, runtime-observed companion to the V1 Product Definition. It shows what
  V1 looks like and how its workflows behave, captured from a safely run instance of
  the application.
</SectionCover>

<MetaPanel items={[
  { label: 'Artefact', value: 'V1 Screenshots & Workflow Guide' },
  { label: 'Companion to', value: 'TACEDGE Ground Engineering V1 Product Definition' },
  { label: 'Runtime', value: 'Local disposable instance · RockControl tenant' },
  { label: 'Data', value: 'Fictional / seeded — no production data' },
  { label: 'Evidence source', value: `${BASELINE.v1Repo} @ <code>${BASELINE.v1ShaShort}</code>` },
  { label: 'Inspection date', value: BASELINE.inspectionDate },
]} />

<h2 id="g-purpose">Purpose &amp; audience</h2>
<p>
  This guide exists to let the incoming Interim Development Technical Lead <em>see</em> V1
  during the V2 scoping sprint: what the screens look like, how a field crew member,
  supervisor and project manager move through the core
  <strong>configure → capture → review → export</strong> chain, and where observed runtime
  behaviour differs from the static Product Definition. It does not repeat the Product
  Definition's full technical detail — it is the picture that sits beside it.
</p>

<Panel title="How this runtime was obtained (safety boundary)" tone="quiet">
  <p>
    tacedge-v1-PD is the only writable repository. TACEDGE Geotech was inspected as a
    strictly read-only evidence source; no intentional changes were made to it. The
    application was run from a <strong>disposable copy of the tracked source</strong> (commit
    <code>{BASELINE.v1ShaShort}</code>) outside both repositories, against a local
    throwaway PostgreSQL seeded with <strong>fictional data</strong> (project "Riverview Cutting
    Stabilisation", client "Alpine Hydro Ltd"). No external service was configured, so no
    email, Teams, SharePoint, voice call or notification could be sent. All accounts are
    fictional fixtures. No credentials appear in this repository.
  </p>
</Panel>

<h2 id="g-classifications">Observation classifications</h2>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Chip</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><span class="rt rt-observed">OBSERVED</span></td><td>Directly seen in the running application.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="rt rt-observed-read-only">OBSERVED — READ ONLY</span></td><td>Seen; no write action performed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="rt rt-observed-test-data">OBSERVED — TEST DATA</span></td><td>Completed using the approved local test data.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="rt rt-partially-observed">PARTIALLY OBSERVED</span></td><td>Part seen; a dependency or safety boundary blocked completion.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="rt rt-blocked">BLOCKED</span></td><td>Could not be inspected (access, integration or safety constraint).</td></tr>
    <tr><td><span class="rt rt-contradicted">CONTRADICTED</span></td><td>Runtime materially differs from the Product Definition.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>

<h2 id="g-limits">Known limitations of this runtime</h2>
<ul>
  <li>One tenant only (RockControl). LPC port, SteepWorks and TACEDGE-brand experiences are BLOCKED — no local data/domains.</li>
  <li>No AI keys: plan import, test-sheet OCR, the engineering test-report PDF, meeting analysis, voice extraction and Ask RC are BLOCKED.</li>
  <li>No map tiles (no LINZ/Mapbox key); no external send (email/Teams/SharePoint/voice).</li>
  <li>Dev server, not the production build; small seeded data volume — not a performance sample.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="g-use">How to use &amp; print</h2>
<p>
  Read the Visual Executive Summary, then the core workflows (WF-01 to WF-10). The
  Screen Atlas is a reference grid; Runtime Validation Findings records where runtime met
  or diverged from the Product Definition. Print the landscape package from
  <a href="/v1-screenshots-workflows/print">/v1-screenshots-workflows/print</a> — browser
  print dialog, A4 <strong>landscape</strong>, background graphics on, save as PDF.
</p>
</section>

<!-- 01 VISUAL EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
<section class={brk} id="g01">
<SectionCover num="01" title="Visual Executive Summary" kicker="What V1 looks like, in one glance">
  The main surfaces and the load-bearing workflow, directly observed.
</SectionCover>
<p>
  V1 runs. From a fresh sign-in it presents a role-adaptive dashboard, a tabbed project
  workspace, a status-coloured anchor plan, a phone-first drill capture screen that
  inherits design presets, a testing register with pass/fail conformance, a Drill Summary
  review table, and a report builder with a live multi-page PDF. The
  <strong>configure → capture → review → export</strong> chain is real and legible.
</p>
<div class="strip">
  <Shot file="/screenshots/v1-workflows/WF-01-S02-dashboard-admin-desktop.png" caption="Configure/monitor — the role-adaptive dashboard." cls="OBSERVED — TEST DATA" />
  <Shot file="/screenshots/v1-workflows/WF-03-S01-anchor-plan-desktop.png" caption="Configure — the schematic Anchor Plan." cls="OBSERVED — TEST DATA" />
  <Shot file="/screenshots/v1-workflows/WF-05-S03-drill-capture-dialog-desktop.png" caption="Capture — drill dialog with design presets inherited." cls="OBSERVED — TEST DATA" />
</div>
<div class="strip">
  <Shot file="/screenshots/v1-workflows/WF-08-S01-drill-summary-desktop.png" caption="Review — Drill Summary (note the empty Review column: no confirm gate)." cls="OBSERVED — TEST DATA" />
  <Shot file="/screenshots/v1-workflows/WF-09-S04-report-builder-desktop.png" caption="Export — Report Builder with a live 28-page PDF preview." cls="OBSERVED — TEST DATA" />
  <Shot file="/screenshots/v1-workflows/WF-01-S05-dashboard-field-mobile.png" caption="Field — the phone-first bottom-nav experience." cls="OBSERVED" viewport="mobile" />
</div>
<Panel title="Most important visual / workflow findings" tone="quiet">
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The configure→capture spine is genuinely present:</strong> design presets flow into the field drill dialog; the operator confirms and records rather than decides.</li>
    <li><strong>There is no confirm/QA gate:</strong> the Drill Summary "Review" column stays empty and export acts on live data — reviewing is not confirming (confirms the PD).</li>
    <li><strong>Outputs are mature:</strong> a 5-sheet drill-log XLSX and a live multi-page engineer report both exist and render.</li>
    <li><strong>Much depends on AI/integrations:</strong> the test-report PDF, OCR, voice and meeting analysis are all disabled without keys — several are load-bearing, not optional.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Unverified:</strong> anything AI-dependent, offline resync, map-with-tiles, and every non-RockControl tenant.</p>
</Panel>
</section>

<!-- 02 ROLE & SURFACE MAP -->
<section class={brk} id="g02">
