</div>
</section>

<!-- 03 SCREEN ATLAS -->
<section class={brk} id="g03">
<SectionCover num="03" title="Screen Atlas" kicker={`${atlas.reduce((n, g) => n + g.entries.length, 0)} screens · every meaningful surface`}>
  A reference grid of every meaningful accessible V1 screen, grouped by area, each with
  its route, screen-sheet ID, role and runtime classification.
</SectionCover>
{atlas.map((group) => (
  <div class="atlas-group">
    <h2 id={`atlas-${group.title.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]+/g, '-')}`}>{group.title}</h2>
    <div class="atlas-grid">
      {group.entries.map((e) => {
        const slug = e.cls.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]+/g, '-').replace(/^-|-$/g, '');
        return (
          <div class="atlas-card">
            {e.file
              ? <div class="thumb"><img src={e.file} alt={e.name} loading="lazy" /></div>
              : <div class="thumb blocked">{e.note || 'BLOCKED'}</div>}
            <div class="atlas-body">
              <h4>{e.name}</h4>
              <div class="atlas-meta">
                <code>{e.route}</code> · {e.pds} · {e.role}<br />
                <span class={`rt rt-${slug}`} style="margin-top:0.35rem">{e.cls}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        );
      })}
    </div>
  </div>
))}
</section>

<!-- 04 CORE WORKFLOWS -->
<section class={brk} id="g04">
<SectionCover num="04" title="Core Ground-Engineering Workflows" kicker="WF-01 to WF-10 · configure → capture → review → export">
  The load-bearing chain, step by step, screenshot-led. These are the workflows most
  relevant to V2 scoping.
</SectionCover>
{P1.map((wf) => <WorkflowSection wf={wf} />)}
</section>

<!-- 05 SAFETY & SUPPORTING -->
<section class={brk} id="g05">
<SectionCover num="05" title="Safety & Supporting Workflows" kicker="WF-11 to WF-16">
  The safety, voice, meeting, forms and mapping workflows that run alongside the core chain.
</SectionCover>
{P2.map((wf) => <WorkflowSection wf={wf} />)}
</section>

<!-- 06 ADMIN & TENANT -->
<section class={brk} id="g06">
<SectionCover num="06" title="Administration & Tenant Workflows" kicker="WF-17 to WF-24 · safely accessible only">
  Administration, integrations and tenant surfaces observed in the local runtime. LPC
  port (WF-22) and the AI assistant (WF-21) were BLOCKED and are recorded as such.
</SectionCover>
{P3.map((wf) => <WorkflowSection wf={wf} />)}
</section>

<!-- 07 CROSS-WORKFLOW FINDINGS -->
<section class={brk} id="g07">
<SectionCover num="07" title="Cross-Workflow Findings" kicker="Patterns across the whole product">
  What repeated across workflows — strengths and V2 scoping risks.
</SectionCover>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Theme</th><th>Observation</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Navigation consistency</td><td>A single, coherent sidebar + top bar across surfaces; role trims are clean; mobile has a purpose-built bottom bar. Consistent and legible.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Role clarity</td><td>The four groups are visibly distinct; Field is meaningfully trimmed. Subcontractor vs FieldTech was not separable at runtime (identical capabilities).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mobile usability</td><td>Capture screens are genuinely phone-first (drill grid, quick-fill, forms, sign-in). Management surfaces are desktop-oriented.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Workflow hand-offs</td><td>Field capture → PM review is live and clear. PM review → outward record is an <em>export</em>, not a hand-off through a confirmed state.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Status &amp; lifecycle</td><td>Anchor status auto-advances and is shown consistently. There is no review-state lifecycle and no confirm gate (RV-02).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Duplicate concepts</td><td>Two capture paths (planned vs "Just Drill"); two document surfaces (project docs vs SharePoint); semi-legacy Jobs/Sites still routed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Customer-specific branching</td><td>In-app brand rendered as TACEDGE for the RockControl tenant locally (RV-12) — a sign of brand resolution leaking beyond config.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Offline behaviour</td><td>Machinery exists (sync queue) but was not exercised; a genuine risk area for the V2 "full shift offline" bar.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Error / empty handling</td><td>Empty and integration-absent states are graceful (Documents, Surveys, Calendar). Form validation blocks incomplete submissions.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Data-entry burden</td><td>Design presets sharply reduce field entry (a real strength). PM setup is spread across many tabs with no guided first-run.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Export dependence</td><td>The outward record is a file. The engineering test-report PDF depends on AI (RV-05) — a reliability coupling worth noting.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Genuine strengths</td><td>Preset inheritance, the status-coloured anchor plan/grid, the XLSX export depth, and the live report-preview builder.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>V2 scoping risks</td><td>No confirm lifecycle; AI in the trusted-record path; tenant branching in code; multiple overlapping models to migrate.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
</section>

<!-- 08 V1->V2 VISUAL ORIENTATION -->
<section class={brk} id="g08">
<SectionCover num="08" title="V1 → V2 Visual Orientation" kicker="Observed V1 beside the V2 reference direction">
  Neutral orientation only — not a delta report. V1 comes from this runtime; V2 comes
  from the reference package.
</SectionCover>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>V1 (observed)</th><th>V2 (reference direction)</th><th>Nature of delta</th><th>Question for the Technical Lead</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Review lifecycle</td><td>Drill Summary reviews; no confirm gate; export on live data (RV-02).</td><td>Two-dimension model: work phase + review state (submitted → confirmed → re-opened); confirmed-only-outward.</td><td>Review lifecycle · data model</td><td>How does the confirm dimension graft onto the flat anchor-log table?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Engineer surface</td><td>ClientViewer read-only role; outward record is an emailed file.</td><td>A glance-first engineer view of confirmed records; QA queue; closeout from the live record.</td><td>UX · workflow</td><td>What server state must exist before an engineer view is honest?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Field capture</td><td>Quick-fill dialog inheriting design presets; status auto-advances.</td><td>Same spine, but capture feeds the confirm lifecycle and a Status Board.</td><td>Workflow</td><td>Does the capture dialog change, or only what happens to its output?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Work types</td><td>Anchors hard-coded end to end.</td><td>Work type = completion-criteria configuration on one spine (anchoring + piling proven).</td><td>Data model · architecture</td><td>Can the anchor schema generalise, or is a work-item abstraction new core?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sign-on</td><td>JSA daily sign-in exists; drilling is NOT gated on it.</td><td>Sign-on gates drilling (SOS-4) — the one enforced barrier.</td><td>Workflow</td><td>Where does the gate live and does V1's form model support it?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>AI</td><td>Broad and often load-bearing (test PDF, OCR, voice, analysis) — disabled without keys.</td><td>Narrow, human-approved: plan import + test conversion; voice a "Should".</td><td>Product scope · reliability</td><td>Which V1 AI features earn a place in V2's propose-approve-commit discipline?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Reporting</td><td>Report Builder with live multi-page PDF + revisions.</td><td>Reporting as release: confirmed records reach the engineer.</td><td>Reporting · workflow</td><td>Does the builder become the closeout tool, or does release-from-record replace it?</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Platform config</td><td>In-app brand leaked to TACEDGE for a non-TACEDGE tenant (RV-12).</td><td>Config-not-code; a clean, documented config boundary.</td><td>Platform configuration</td><td>Where must the tenant-config boundary sit to stop brand/logic leaking into code?</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
</section>

