<h2 id="g-a-blocked">C. Blocked / uncaptured</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>BLOCKED workflows:</strong> WF-21 (Ask RC assistant — no AI key), WF-22 (LPC port experience — no tenant/domain).</li>
  <li><strong>BLOCKED actions within workflows:</strong> AI plan import &amp; job brief (WF-03), test-sheet OCR &amp; test-report PDF (WF-07), voice extraction (WF-13), meeting recording/analysis (WF-14), map tiles (WF-16), SharePoint browse (WF-20), drone worker (WF-23), Outlook connect (WF-24).</li>
  <li><strong>Tenant variants not captured:</strong> LPC port, SteepWorks, and full TACEDGE-brand (only the host-fallback shell was seen).</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="g-a-method">D. Capture &amp; sanitisation methodology</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Runtime:</strong> disposable copy of TACEDGE Geotech @ <code>{BASELINE.v1ShaShort}</code>, local PostgreSQL 16 on 127.0.0.1:5433, seeded by the repo's own <code>seed-local.cjs</code> with names further fictionalised. Server: <code>npm run dev</code> on :5000.</li>
  <li><strong>Automation:</strong> Puppeteer (Chromium) capture scripts in <code>tools/</code> — deterministic viewports (1440×900 desktop, 390×844 mobile), animations disabled, session cookies from throwaway local accounts (never committed). Scripts never send communications or create production records.</li>
  <li><strong>Sanitisation:</strong> all data is fictional/seeded, so screenshots needed no redaction; each was reviewed before inclusion. Raw captures live in the gitignored <code>working/</code>; only reviewed images are in <code>public/screenshots/v1-workflows/</code>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="g-a-baseline">E. Runtime &amp; repository baseline</h2>
<MetaPanel items={[
  { label: 'Evidence source', value: `${BASELINE.v1Repo} @ <code>${BASELINE.v1Sha}</code>` },
  { label: 'Runtime', value: 'Local disposable · PostgreSQL 16 · Node dev server' },
